+  - Five of them are hooks that read a JSON payload from stdin and take no command-line arguments: `boundary-check`, `loop-guard`, `permission-guard`, `session-start`, `shell-guard`. Their docstring describes the hook contract instead of a usage line. They are still commands, and their docstring is their entry.
+
+**Import side effects (checked).** Importing any of the seven argparse programs runs only definitions and constant assignments. Examples: `NO_WINDOW = subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW if sys.platform == "win32" else 0`, compiled regexes, `HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))`, and `evaluate-reports.py`'s `HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")`. Stream reconfiguration happens only in the `__main__` blocks. Two hand-parsed programs, `bridge-run.py` and `roster-check.py`, run `sys.path.insert(0, HERE)` and `import bridge_env` at import. That is why the generator must not import hand-parsed programs (Requirement 4). The existing tests load programs by file through `tests/conftest.py`'s `load_program(name)` (`importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` then `exec_module`). That is the established way to import a dash-named program.
